mpt-launched Memory panel lets a user browse, add, modify, and[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]delete SASE memory notes for any memory-bearing scope, defaulting [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]to the current project, with parent/child link travel and a publish[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]step that keeps AGENTS.md and provider shims in sync.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]ace_memory_panel.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/ace_memory_panel.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-qt[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-qt/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory scope ring and snapshot service[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-catalog: build the scope ring, cached per-scope note snapshots, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the note tree, and the generated-note contract the panel reads.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared memory-note mutation engine[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-writes[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-writes: add a CLI-free create/update/delete engine for memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes with pure validation, atomic writes, a stale-write guard, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete backups.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ace.keymaps.memory binding scope[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-keymaps[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-keymaps: register the panel-scoped keymap dataclass, defaults, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config schema, binding builders, and app help sections.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory panel shell, note tree, filter, and scope switching[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-shell[dim] · [dim][/dim]after memory-catalog, panel-keymaps[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-shell: build the modal, the nested note rail, the note card, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]filtering, scope cycling and picking, empty/error states, and passive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]open/copy actions.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Parent and child link travel[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-links[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-links: add the numbered PARENT/CHILDREN chips, chip cursor, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbered follow, and the bounded breadcrumb trail with back travel.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Add, edit, delete, and publish surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel-mutations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell, memory-writes[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel-mutations: wire the add/edit forms, the delete confirmation, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tracked-proc writes, and the sase memory init publish flow with its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unpublished state.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Prompt gm and Ctrl+G m entry point[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]prompt-entry[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-entry: claim the prompt g-prefix m continuation, post the request[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]message, open the panel seeded from the memory reference under the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cursor, and restore focus.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation, visual snapshots, and full verification[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-panel-verification[dim] · [dim][/dim]after panel-links, panel-mutations, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]prompt-entry[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-panel-verification: document the panel and its keymap scope, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]PNG snapshot goldens, and run the exhaustive verification lanes.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-qt","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-qt.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-2794e462f423eccc829b84bca1229308","started_at":"2026-08-19T12:18:01.738107+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"395f83f50acaae0c34b57bea582c55e8def5a902557b41b114c44e58e898aac4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qt.6/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"579e0219c791a93201c08e402572e3f0acebc95d411be653050d2417c5bf628a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qt.6/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"92f3b25ee375fa89b1248131ad35c1ec15980fc72e7b1aa7f54ef91a626104a7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qt.6/prompt.md","size_bytes":170},"state":{"digest":"4a1ed5963e87e04832baf519d516d241c9253eca0f82483b26338e5f5843f430","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qt.6/state.json","size_bytes":16